---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — WaveCheck"
  description="How WaveCheck collects, uses, and protects your personal information."
  ogType="article"
  ogTitle="WaveCheck Privacy Policy"
  ogDescription="How WaveCheck collects, uses, and protects your personal information."
  theme="light"
  bodyClass="bg-white text-primary-900 min-h-screen flex flex-col"
>
  <main class="flex-1">
    <section class="bg-gradient-to-b from-primary-50 to-white">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-12 pb-4 sm:pt-16 sm:pb-6">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-premium-600 uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">Privacy</p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-2 pb-10 space-y-10">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">1. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p class="text-primary-600 leading-relaxed">We collect the following information when you use WaveCheck:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-primary-600 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
          <li>Account information you provide: name, username, email, authentication credentials, profile photo, and bio.</li>
          <li>Your date of birth, which we use to confirm you meet our minimum age requirement.</li>
          <li>Content you upload: photos, videos, and the wave, weather, and ocean conditions you log, along with the surf spot you select for each report.</li>
          <li>Device and usage data: device type, operating system, app version, IP address, crash logs, and basic interaction events used to diagnose issues and improve the app.</li>
          <li>Push notification token: if you grant notification permission, we store a token issued by Apple or Google so we can deliver alerts.</li>
          <li>Shipping address: if you redeem a reward that is posted to you, we store the recipient name and postal address you provide. We use it only to send what you redeemed, we do not share it with anyone beyond the postal or courier service handling that delivery, and it is deleted when you delete your account. You can change or remove it at any time.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3 text-primary-600 leading-relaxed">We do not track your device location in the background.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <p class="text-primary-600 leading-relaxed">We use your information to operate the platform, display your posts and profile to other users, send notifications you have opted into, prevent abuse and enforce our Terms of Service, and diagnose technical issues.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">3. How We Share &amp; Store Your Data</h2>
        <p class="text-primary-600 leading-relaxed">We do not sell your personal data. We share data with the cloud infrastructure and service providers who help us run WaveCheck — including database, authentication, and file storage providers — and with Apple and Google for app distribution, push notifications, and in-app billing. We may also disclose information if required by law or to protect the safety of our users.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-primary-600 leading-relaxed">WaveCheck is operated from Australia, and your data is stored and processed on servers located in Australia. If you access WaveCheck from outside Australia, your information is transferred to and stored in Australia, which may have data-protection laws different from those in your country. We take reasonable steps to keep it protected in line with this policy.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">4. Data Security</h2>
        <p class="text-primary-600 leading-relaxed">We implement appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect your personal information from unauthorised access, alteration, or destruction. No system is perfectly secure, however, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">5. Your Rights</h2>
        <p class="text-primary-600 leading-relaxed">You have the right to access, correct, or delete your personal data. You can manage most of this directly in your account settings, or contact us at <a href="mailto:support@wavecheck.app" class="text-premium-600 hover:underline">support@wavecheck.app</a> for assistance.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-primary-600 leading-relaxed">We retain your personal data for as long as your account is active and delete it when you delete your account.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">6. Children’s Privacy</h2>
        <p class="text-primary-600 leading-relaxed">WaveCheck is not intended for users under the age of 16. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 16. If we become aware that we have collected information from a user under 16, we will delete the account and associated data.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">7. Contact Us</h2>
        <p class="text-primary-600 leading-relaxed">If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at <a href="mailto:support@wavecheck.app" class="text-premium-600 hover:underline">support@wavecheck.app</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <p class="text-xs text-primary-400 pt-4">Last updated: September 2026</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
